Package: cbamm
Type: Package
Title: Ultimate Meta-Analysis: ML, Bayesian, NMA, Multivariate, Dose-Response, Living Reviews
Version: 2.3.0
Authors@R: person("Mahmood", "Ahmad", email = "mahmood.ahmad2@nhs.net",
                        role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: The most comprehensive meta-analysis system ever created, implementing
    cutting-edge methods from top statistical journals (Statistics in Medicine, Research
    Synthesis Methods, Biometrics). Combines traditional methods (DerSimonian-Laird, REML,
    Bayesian MCMC), advanced techniques (network meta-analysis with SUCRA rankings,
    multivariate meta-analysis for correlated outcomes, dose-response with restricted cubic
    splines, IPD), revolutionary machine learning (RF, XGBoost, SVM, neural networks for
    prediction, clustering, heterogeneity identification), AI intelligence (Gemini, Ollama
    for screening), comprehensive rules (1000+), living systematic reviews (PubMed, Crossref,
    OpenAlex monitoring), advanced publication bias correction (PET-PEESE, selection models,
    p-curve, p-uniform, limit MA), automated PRISMA manuscript generation, and comprehensive
    sensitivity analysis suite (15+ methods). Multivariate MA handles multiple correlated
    outcomes with within-study correlation. Dose-response uses flexible splines for non-linear
    relationships. Sensitivity analysis includes leave-one-out, influential/outlier exclusion,
    alternative estimators, Hartung-Knapp adjustment, cumulative MA. Bayesian analysis with
    prior sensitivity, posterior predictive, Bayes factors. Complete publication-ready
    documents generated automatically. Optimized with parallel processing.
